proof.text:
For any $L\in D^+(S_e,A)$ choose a lower bound for $L$. Step 5 preserves this bound under $c_{e,*},u_{e,!}$ and either further extension $v_{e,!},i_{e,*}$. The same holds for $H$ by Step 10. The closed immersions $c,i$ are quasi-compact by Steps 1--4 and separated by [lem-weil-pbc-separated-cancellation], hence quasi-separated by [lem-pc-separated-quasi-separated]. Thus [prop-weil-pbc-comparison-direct-image] is defined for $c$ at $L,H$, giving $
u_V^*Rc_{e,*}L\cong Rc_{p,*}
u_S^*L$ and the same formula for $H$. It is also defined for $i$ at $u_{e,!}L,u_{e,!}H$, which are bounded below, and gives $
u_T^*Ri_{e,*}u_{e,!}L\cong Ri_{p,*}
u_{ ar S}^*u_{e,!}L$, likewise for $H$. More generally the open immersions $u,v$ are quasi-compact and separated by the same geometry, so the cited comparison can be applied at every intervening bounded-below source as well. This verifies the domain assertion after either factorization of the immersion.
